-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile: text file which consist of set of instructions required to create a custom image.
instructions:
FROM : ur dockerfile always atrts with FROM . it consist of the base image of the container.
  eg - FROM ubuntu | FROM jenkins

RUN : we can install any packages & s/w inside container.
   eg - RUN apt update | Run apt install apache -y | Run touch file | RUN rm /var/www/html/index.html

COPY : if u want to copy some file from the machine to the container when it is created
   eg - COPY vip.txt /tmp/
            { vip.txt = source location | tmp = destination inside )

EXPOSE : here u can define on which port the app is running , it helps the devops to do port mapping (-p)
   eg - EXPOSE 8080 

CMD : whatever will be written after CMD will be executed a container runtime, lets suppose u want to start some package when container is running
   eg - CMD apachectl -d FORGROUND
